# M11 regression: three debris objects share a 120 km home orbit with a tanker. It grabs one with the claw, deorbits it and lets go,
# completing a cleanup contract; the other two decay on their own over the following days. Test tool only (decision #16).
tutorial 11
spawn clawtanker Sweeper orbit 120000 phase 0 fuel 1
stage
spawn junk Junk1 orbit 120000 phase -0.03 fuel 0
spawn junk Junk2 orbit 57000 phase 40 fuel 0
spawn junk Junk3 orbit 58000 phase 80 fuel 0
active Sweeper
expect debris == 3
contract debris 1
accept Clean
expect contracts_active == 1
target Junk1
tap rcs
attitude target
approach on
until docked_debris >= 1 timeout 900
approach off
attitude off
expect docked_debris == 1 and debris == 2
view zoom 8
shot debris-grabbed
log grabbed
# Retrograde burn until the periapsis is deep in the atmosphere, then release the junk on its way down.
attitude retrograde
wait 8
tap throttle_full
until peri < 20000 timeout 120
tap throttle_cut
attitude off
undock
until docked_debris == 0 timeout 5
expect debris == 3
# Save the sweeper: prograde burn back to a safe periapsis while the junk continues down.
attitude prograde
wait 8
tap throttle_full
until peri > 60000 timeout 120
tap throttle_cut
attitude off
expect peri > 60000
warp 3
until contracts_done == 1 timeout 200000
warp 0
expect contracts_done == 1 and debris == 2
log cleaned
# Decay: the two low pieces (periapsis under 1.2 × the 50 km atmosphere) sink and burn up over the following days.
warp 6
until debris == 0 timeout 1728000
warp 0
expect debris == 0
log decayed
end
